      "pending_request_handling": {
        "mode": "eof_unobservable",
        "trigger": "literal_port_disconnect",
        "per_request_outcome": "unknown",
        "host_correlated_cancellation_claim": "forbidden",
        "synthesized_port_closed": "local_only_never_host_proof",
        "rationale": "Option 2 (user decision 2026-11-02): an abrupt EOF on the Native Messaging pipe (literal port.disconnect(), connector tab close, Chrome-owned pipe closure) leaves no channel on which the host's per-request terminal events can be observed: the connector is detached and Chrome owns the pipe. The individual pending request's outcome is therefore recorded as unknown / not observable. The connector's own synthesized internal/port_closed is local only and is never evidence that the host cancelled anything. This case verifies process exit and OS BLE link release for both phones only."
      }
